5.4 The Contractor warrants that it is not, and will not become, a related body corporate of NCRMG, and that no director or officer of the Contractor is a director or officer of NCRMG.

5.5 The Contractor shall ensure that any subcontractor engaged in accordance with clause 2.4:

(a) provides a written undertaking to the Contractor that it will comply with the Contractor's obligations under this Agreement to the extent applicable to its scope of work;

(b) is covered by the Contractor's public liability and workers compensation insurance policies, or maintains equivalent cover of its own; and

(c) has not been the subject of a finding of non-compliance under the Modern Slavery Act 2018 (Cth) within the preceding three years.

**6. Maintenance Standards and Network Access**

6.1 The Services shall be performed in accordance with:

(a) the Maintenance Plan set out in Schedule 1 and any amendments to it approved in writing by NCRMG;

(b) the NCRMG Network Rules and Procedures, as amended from time to time;

(c) the applicable Australian Standards, including AS 7631 for the management of rail infrastructure assets; and

(d) all directions issued by the Network Operations Manager under clause 2.3.

6.2 The Contractor shall comply with the NCRMG Rail Corridor Access Protocol when entering the Network, including:

(a) booking all track possession and protection requirements through the NCRMG Track Access Portal no later than 48 hours before the proposed access;

(b) nominating a competent person to act as the Contractor's Site Controller for each work site; and

